A Mac set to Europe/Istanbul names its Windows time zone Turkey Standard Time,
not Arab Standard Time.

Wine picks the registry time zone whose rules match the host for the current
year, taking the first match in the registry's order. Nine zones are UTC+3
without daylight saving time today, and Arab Standard Time (Riyadh) comes
first, so Turkey, Russia, Jordan, Syria, Kenya and Belarus all reported
Riyadh. Rockstar's sign in refuses a client whose time zone disagrees with
where it connects from: the Rockstar Games Launcher answered #1.000.7 (and
#1.500.7 for a new account) to two players in Turkey whose accounts signed in
from a Mac browser (highball#477, highball#478). Deleting the seven UTC+3
zones listed before Turkey Standard Time from the prefix made Wine report
Turkey Standard Time, and the launcher then signed in (confirmed by the
reporter of highball#477, M1 Max, macOS 27.0.1, engine
x64-crossover26.3-r27).

CrossOver's tree already tells some same-rule zones apart in match_tz_name:
by the host's zone abbreviation and, where those agree, by the host's offset
at a past date (Korea and North Korea, Tokyo and Yakutsk). The UTC+3 zones go
in the same table. Turkey was UTC+2 until September 2016, Jordan and Syria
until October 2022, Riyadh, Baghdad and Minsk were UTC+3 at both dates, and
Moscow (MSK) and Nairobi (EAT) have abbreviations of their own.

Checked 2026-10-24 on macOS 27 with a C program that copies match_tz_name and
match_past_tz_bias over the nine zones in registry order: Europe/Istanbul gets
Turkey Standard Time; Asia/Riyadh, Asia/Qatar, Asia/Baghdad and Europe/Minsk
keep Arab Standard Time as before; Africa/Nairobi and Africa/Addis_Ababa get
E. Africa Standard Time; Asia/Amman and Asia/Damascus get Jordan Standard
Time; Europe/Moscow, Europe/Volgograd and Europe/Simferopol get Russian
Standard Time. Upstream Wine has no such table; not sent.

